      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ANI/status/2023046273012752537",
      "text": "#WATCH | Delhi | On preparation for AI Impact Summit, Additional CP Traffic, Dinesh Kumar Gupta says, \"The Delhi Traffic Police has issued a traffic advisory regarding the AI ​​Impact Summit, scheduled to be held from February 16 to 20. The event will be held at Bharat Mandapam... Traffic will be affected on several major roads, including Mathura Road (from Subramanian Bharti Marg to Lodhi Road Flyover), Akbar Road, Janpath, Shanti Path, Satya Marg, Africa Avenue, APJ Abdul Kalam Road, Tilak Marg, Bhagwan Das Road... Access to the airport and railway stations will remain, but passengers are advised to leave early. Board exams are scheduled for 10 schools on the VVIP route, starting February 17th. The traffic police have deployed special nodal officers for these schools to ensure students do not face any difficulties reaching the exam centres...\"",
